imagine the lego movie and Deadpool got  together and had a PG rated love child  well they kind of did  it's the Lego Batman movie yippee-ki-yay  movie lovers it's Jan here if you're a  Batman fan then you'll quite likely feel  you've died and gone to bat heaven when  you watch the latest entry in the lego  movie franchise with other fish to fry  hello han solo movie lego movie  directors Phil Lord and Christopher  Miller handed the directing reins for  this film over to Chris McKay who edited  and co-directed animation on the first  movie  McKay's production is a crazy colorful  irreverent ball of energy that races  through the Caped Crusader's many and  varied incarnations over the years while  weaving in a story of family and team  spirit that occasionally veers into  sentimentality never afraid to poke fun  at itself the bat Legacy movie cliches  or the movie business in general the  Lego Batman movie channels a spirit of  2014 super successful lego movie and  throws into the mix the kind of barrage  of meta gags and endless Easter eggs so  wickedly brought to life in Ryan  Reynolds Deadpool movie in fact you'll  need more than one viewing to catch all  of them and of course this being a  Batman movie there's plenty of what  you'd expect including tricked-out  vehicles and costumes an explosive  action will arnett returns as Batman  after debuting his own gravelly voice to  take on the character in the first lego  movie I loved Arness as Joe bin Arrested  Development and Devon in 30 rock and he  certainly puts his comedy chops to good  use here proving yet again that he was  the right choice for the part of a  preposterously pompous Dark Knight who's  in dire need of having his posturing  taken down a peg or two  as for the supporting cast Arnett's  Arrested Development co-star Michael  Cera gives an amusingly enthusiastic  performance as Batman fanboy and  sidekick Robin while ray Fiennes is  fantastic as Batman's Butler alfred  rosario Dawson puts in a nice turn as  Barbara Gordon jumping across to the  world of DC from the MCU where she's  usually found as nurse Claire temple in  Marvel's Netflix shows and as the voice  of the Joker Zach Galifianakis gives the  perfectly serviceable performance though  I doubt it'll stay with you in the way  say that Mark Hamill's does on top of  the main players as a ton of cameos  including loads of comic-book characters  as well as a varied bunch of individuals  from the wider world of movies and  literature and I'll have a video on that  soon as well as the movies cool  connections and Easter eggs now if  you're thinking this movie is  essentially one big  foreleg oh well in many ways you're not  wrong but there's certainly enough fun  substance and gorgeous visuals in the  film to mean it's more than just a  platter to serve up merchandise the one  thing I did find a little grating was  the amount of over-the-top product  placement for a certain smartphone if  you're looking for a loss of brick  building like in the first movie you  won't find it here which makes sense  because construction was a big part of  the actual story in the lego movie  whereas here it isn't and that didn't  bother me at all to be honest with you  oh and you won't find a song either with  the same level of earworm eNOS as  everything is awesome which in some ways  is no bad thing instead the soundtrack  uses 80's pop too often comical effect  and composer Lorne Balfe does a nice job  integrating some rather familiar  superhero themes into his score to sum  up the Lego Batman movie does a good job  continuing the entertaining franchise  kick started three years ago by Phil  Lord and Chris Miller it's fun often  funny silly and crammed full of cameos  connections and Easter eggs to the Caped  Crusader's world as well as a DC  Universe and beyond yes it does  sometimes indulge in sentimentality much  as its predecessor did but there's much  to enjoy in Chris McKay spin off and as  it's the first superhero movie housed in  a packed year of super flicks I'm glad  to say we're off to a good start  fingers crossed things carry on that way  now what did you think of the Lego  Batman movie and who are your favorite  DC superheroes and villains let me know  in the comments below  coming up I've got a Lego Batman Easter  egg video and videos on the DC TV shows  Supergirl arrow and the flash if you  enjoyed this video do share it and  subscribe for more movie reviews Easter  eggs and crazy movie and TV facts thanks  for watching and see you next time you  pka movie lovers
 

